WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.120
Glad to have you with us on Tesla's short time. Episode 548. It's July 21st, 2026,

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.080
and I'm Patrick and Vancouver. Let's get into what's moving in the Tesla world today.

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:18.340
Starlink V5's roof integration in the CyberCab requires a full redesign of thermal

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:24.900
paths and pressure vents that would otherwise limit robotaxi uptime. The CyberCab becomes the first

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:30.800
Tesla model confirmed to carry the integrated Starlink V5 terminal inside the roof cavity,

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:37.820
rather than as an external dish. Integration replaces the traditional metal roof section with a radio

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:44.680
frequency transparent polymer cover and a multi-layer antenna stack beneath it. A shock noted that

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:50.360
the connection focuses on allowing Tesla to reach vehicles and riders directly while tracking fleet

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:56.740
performance data for operational oversight. The design draws on SpaceX patents that describe

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:03.880
a 90% air honeycomb spacer, dual patch antennas, and copper thermal rims to move heat to the outer

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:10.440
surface. Passive cooling, micro vents, and floating snap fits handle expansion mismatch and pressure

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:16.780
changes during altitude shifts without fans or heaters. This architecture supports both fleet

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:23.020
telemetry and future passenger connectivity, once unsupervised robotaxi operations begin.

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:30.200
Production of the CyberCab is already in pilot at a roughly 2 million unit annual target once scaled.

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.060
While the hardware team solves these integration challenges, the supervised autonomy software

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:43.940
continues its own rapid iteration cycle. Tesla has begun distributing the FSDV-14 light build

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:50.380
beyond the initial small group. The AI chief hinted the version may soon reach a broader release

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:56.840
under the established supervised cadence. Multiple reports show birds flying directly across the

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:05.120
path of a vehicle running FSDV-14.3.5, with no braking response or avoidance maneuver recorded.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:11.620
The observer noted the system showed no flinch during those crossings. Regulators still require

00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:18.260
human oversight for city street operation, while HW-5 development remains on a separate track.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:23.740
Watch for whether later point releases at explicit bird or small object handling.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:30.160
The light rollout follows the established cadence of supervised releases, moving the program forward

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:36.800
on data collection and refinement. The same supervised testing that surfaces these edge cases is also

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:42.580
drawing attention from cities and first responders. First responders in Austin report ongoing

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:49.200
difficulties interacting with Tesla robot taxis during incidents. Local rules give cities limited

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:55.260
authority to impose new operating conditions on the vehicles. The issue surfaces as supervised

00:02:55.260 --> 00:03:02.840
FSD continues wider testing with no unsupervised deployment date set. Watch for whether state legislation

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:10.260
changes the regulatory tools available to cities. Supervised FSD testing in Austin fits the pattern

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:17.380
of gradual geographic expansion seen in prior releases. On the positive side, Tesla's current vehicle

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:23.840
lineup continues to show strength in key markets. The model Y is positioned to finish as the top

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:30.520
selling vehicle in Europe for June. The Dacia Sandero remains the year-to-date leader across all

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:38.720
power trains. Tesla's European volume continues to draw from Giga Berlin output. June EV sales across

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:46.120
the region rose 52% year-over-year. The model Y and Model 3 accounted for a large share of that growth.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:52.180
The increase comes despite broader industry production adjustments. Giga Berlin production

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:58.280
supports the model Y's European position while the broader EV segment shows renewed growth after

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:04.580
earlier adjustments. Model Y also features an automatic seat and liftgate reversal when an

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:10.600
obstruction is detected during powered movement. The system prevents damage to the vehicle or items

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:16.820
during passenger loading. It uses the same sensor arrays already present for other safety functions.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:23.260
The capability arrives through an over-the-air software update. Similar reversal logic may appear

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:29.880
later on additional closures or body panels. Source material lists the announcement directly from Tesla.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:36.020
X-Pang Australia plans multiple new models aimed at Tesla and Zeaker buyers in that market.

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:40.560
The lineup includes vehicles positioned directly against the Model Y.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:45.100
Local launch timing and pricing details remain under wraps for now.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:51.440
The strategy expands X-Pang's presence in right-hand drive markets. Watch for the first Australian

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:57.500
customer deliveries once the models arrive. The planned vehicles target the segment where the model Y

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:05.140
has held strong volume. A driver built a painted brick wall illusion on the road to test autopilot detection

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:11.040
at highway speeds. The test checks whether the vision system treats the image as a real obstacle.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:18.480
Results remain anecdotal and unverified by Tesla. The experiment highlights ongoing public scrutiny

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:24.820
of supervised autonomy limits. Watch for any official Tesla response on edge case handling.

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:31.100
The test adds to a pattern of independent checks on vision-only performance that continue while the

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:37.560
supervised system iterates. Bayzenar highlights six specific updates on the refreshed Model S and

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:44.040
Model X signature addition. The changes focus on interior materials, lighting and wheel designs.

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:50.960
Production continues at Fremont alongside other sedan and SUV lines. The additions sit at

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:57.660
the top of the current S and X range. Watch for owner feedback on the new trim details once deliveries

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:04.060
begin. The signature addition updates arrive as the S and X maintain their position as the

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:11.100
premium end of Tesla's Fremont built lineup. Bayzenar lists five observable details from a

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:17.500
cyber cab sighting at San Francisco International Airport. The vehicle showed the expected roof line

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:23.780
and sensor layout from the Wii Robot reveal. No passengers were present during the observed movement.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:30.040
The sighting adds to early real world visibility of the platform. Watch for additional airport or

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:36.080
fleet testing locations. The SFO appearance fits the pattern of early public sightings that have

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:42.180
followed the Wii Robot unveiling while production remains in pilot phase. Tesla's Giga Berlin

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:48.440
operations have added jobs while other German automakers cut positions. The plant continues to

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:55.000
support Model Y production for European and export markets. Employment growth occurs against a

00:06:55.000 --> 00:07:01.540
backdrop of broader industry restructuring. Output remains tied to demand signals and regulatory

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:08.820
approvals. Watch for the next quarterly employment or production update from the site. Giga Berlin's

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:14.020
employment trajectory continues the factory's established role in Tesla's European manufacturing

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:21.120
footprint even as competitors reduce headcount. Even as vehicle demand holds up, investors are

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:27.520
watching the spending side of the business closely. Tesla's heavy spending on AI infrastructure is

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:33.720
expected to push cash flow negative in coming quarters. The company continues to fund Cortex

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:40.380
clusters and Dojo scale training while vehicle margins face pressure. Investors will watch whether

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:47.140
the spending produces measurable progress on unsupervised FSD or Optimus before the next capital

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:53.020
raise. The upcoming earnings report will give the first clear view of the burn rate trajectory.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:08:00.380
Cortex and Dojo investments remain central to the long-term capability targets for both FSD and

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:06.620
Optimus. Vehicle roofs have always been treated as simple structural panels whose main job is

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:12.780
to keep weather out and passengers in. Once a satellite terminal must live inside that same panel,

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:18.980
every material choice suddenly carries thermal, RF, and pressure consequences that no traditional

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:25.240
stamp steel roof was ever designed to handle. The cyber cab solution replaces the metal with a

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:31.840
polymer cover and then builds an entire multi-layer antenna stack beneath it, complete with 90% air

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:37.720
spacers and copper heat spreading rims that move waste energy to the outer surface without fans or

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:44.060
heaters. The same stack must also survive daily altitude changes that expand trapped air inside

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:51.180
the honeycomb cells. Engineers therefore added intercellular micro vents and a floating snap fit chassis

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:57.800
so the assembly can breathe and shift without delaminating. Those vents and compliant adhesives add

00:08:57.800 --> 00:09:03.280
cost and assembly steps, yet they remove the need for separate active heating elements that would

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:10.100
otherwise drain the robotaxi's battery on cold mornings. The net result is a roof that performs three

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:17.000
unrelated functions, structural cover, thermal radiator, and satellite aperture while adding minimal

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:23.440
mass or power draw. That multifunction approach changes the unit economics of the vehicle itself.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:29.720
Every watt saved on heating or every kilogram avoided in the roof improves range and therefore

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:36.160
revenue per trip for a fleet operator. The engineering investment is front loaded but the recurring

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:42.220
saving scale with every vehicle produced. The open question is whether the same roof architecture

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:48.580
can be adapted to lower volume models without the same cost amortization or whether it remains a

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:55.480
cyber cab specific solution until volumes justify broader use. Keep an eye on Q2 earnings for the

00:09:55.480 --> 00:10:02.080
first detailed look at how cortex and dojo spending affects near-term cash flow. That covers it for

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:14.680
today's Tesla developments. TSLA closed at $369.57, down $11.27, 3%. Share this episode with a

